{"id":2355,"date":"2026-08-27T17:57:36","date_gmt":"2026-08-27T17:57:36","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/?post_type=knowledgebase&#038;p=2355"},"modified":"2026-08-27T18:15:57","modified_gmt":"2026-08-27T18:15:57","slug":"quick-rounded-corners","status":"publish","type":"knowledgebase","link":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/db\/graphics\/quick-rounded-corners\/","title":{"rendered":"Quick Rounded Corners"},"content":{"rendered":"<div style=\"color: #2b2b2b;\">\n<h2 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Quick Rounded Corners<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-2367\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/QuickRoundedCorners.webp\" alt=\"Quick Rounded Corners\" width=\"262\" height=\"174\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/QuickRoundedCorners.webp 1423w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/QuickRoundedCorners-300x199.webp 300w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/QuickRoundedCorners-1024x679.webp 1024w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/QuickRoundedCorners-768x509.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 262px) 100vw, 262px\" \/><\/span><\/h2>\n<p class=\"western\">You can instantly soften the edges of any picture in your document using the <strong>Quick Rounded Corners<\/strong> tool. This provides a fast way to apply modern, curved edges to your photos without needing to manually draw shapes or open complex masking menus.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Applying Rounded Corners<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-2360\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/RoundedCorners-1.webp\" alt=\"Applying Rounded Corners\" width=\"400\" height=\"543\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/RoundedCorners-1.webp 525w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/RoundedCorners-1-221x300.webp 221w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Select the image you want to modify on your canvas.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Right-click<\/strong> the image to open the context menu.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Hover over <strong>Rounded Corners<\/strong> to reveal the flyout menu.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Select your desired corner radius: <strong>8px<\/strong> (subtle), <strong>16px<\/strong> (standard), <strong>24px<\/strong> (soft), or <strong>32px<\/strong> (pill-like).<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p class=\"western\">The corners will instantly apply to the image. Because this is a <strong>non-destructive crop<\/strong>, your original image data is preserved perfectly. You can change the radius at any time, or remove it entirely, without losing any quality or cutting off your picture permanently.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">The Crop to Shape Modal<\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">The four rounded corner presets are also fully integrated into the main <strong>Crop to Shape<\/strong> modal. If you prefer working from the ribbon instead of the right-click menu:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Select your image.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Navigate to the <strong>Picture Tools<\/strong> contextual tab.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Click <strong>Crop to Shape<\/strong>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-2364\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheCropToShapeModal.webp\" alt=\"The Crop to Shape Modal\" width=\"221\" height=\"197\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheCropToShapeModal.webp 524w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheCropToShapeModal-300x267.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 221px) 100vw, 221px\" \/><\/h3>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">You will find the new rounded rectangle presets prominently listed alongside the other standard shapes.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Quick Rounded Corners You can instantly soften the edges of any picture in your document using the Quick Rounded Corners tool. This provides a fast way to apply modern, curved edges to your photos without needing to manually draw shapes or open complex masking menus. Applying Rounded Corners Select the image you want to modify [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":2367,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","template":"","knowledgebase_cat":[13],"class_list":["post-2355","knowledgebase","type-knowledgebase","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","knowledgebase_cat-graphics"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2355","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/knowledgebase"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2355"}],"version-history":[{"count":9,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2355\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2373,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2355\/revisions\/2373"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2367"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2355"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"knowledgebase_cat","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase_cat?post=2355"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}